nstall since nothing deploys the file."},{"label":"New check-rules bin","description":"Landing C: dedicated bin/check-rules.js, still on demand but runnable from a shell (exit codes mirror trust-hook)."}],"multiSelect":false},{"question":"Only if 'Keep on demand': how much wording to change?","header":"Wording","options":[{"label":"Full record (Recommended)","description":"Tick entry; JSDoc 'yet' → on-demand reason; 'kept on demand' on POC row 3, L566, BACKLOG L1273–1277; append empty-file fact to deploy-step entry."},{"label":"Minimal","description":"Same, minus the JSDoc edit and the deploy-entry sentence."},{"label":"Full + README","description":"Full record plus a README sentence showing how to run the check (README never documents deploying the file)."}],"multiSelect":false},{"question":"Only if wired (trust-hook or new bin): what happens when the deployed rules file is absent?","header":"Absent file","options":[{"label":"Report, no outcome change (Recommended)","description":"Warn 'not installed'; trust outcome unchanged (new bin: exit 1)."},{"label":"Refuse, exit 2","description":"As the original B9 plan said; breaks trust-hook on every documented install today."},{"label":"Split by mode","description":"Report in write mode, exit 1 from --check; breaks the '--check refuses exactly what write mode refuses' rule."}],"multiSelect":false},{"question":"Only if wired into trust-hook: which modes run the check?","header":"Modes","options":[{"label":"Both, before any write (Recommended)","description":"After the listing-complete check, before the mode split; drift blocks trusting the hook until the file is re-copied."},{"label":"--check only","description":"Write mode never looks at rules."},{"label":"Both, trust first","description":"Write mode saves trust, then exits 2 on drift."}],"multiSelect":false}]}}}
